UPDATE questions SET stem_html='<h3>Passage</h3><p>Jamaican British artist Willard Wigan is known for his remarkable so small that they are best viewed through a microscope, Wigan&#x27;s sculptures are made from tiny natural materials, such as spiderweb strands.</p><h3>Question</h3><p>Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?</p>', choices_json='[{"letter": "A", "content": "<p>microsculptures creations</p>"}, {"letter": "B", "content": "<p>microsculptures, creations</p>"}, {"letter": "C", "content": "<p>microsculptures. Creations</p>"}, {"letter": "D", "content": "<p>microsculptures and creations</p>"}]', explanation_html=NULL, stem_text='A student tracked spider populations in two outdoor enclosures over 30 days — one containing lizards, one without them. Observing that the spider count in the lizard enclosure fell sharply over the period, the student concluded that the decline was entirely attributable to predation by the lizards.
Which choice best describes data that, if true, would weaken the student''s conclusion?' WHERE id='nx_3af5a62034e78102ad5ad11aaef44253';
UPDATE questions SET stem_html='<p>The Post Office is a 1912 play by Rabindranath Tagore. Amal imagines people passing his window are carefree even when working, as when he says to a flower seller''s daughter: ______ Which quotation from The Post Office most effectively illustrates the claim?</p>', choices_json='[{"id":"A","content":"“I see, you don’t wish to stop; I don’t care to stay on here either.”"},{"id":"B","content":"“Oh, flower gathering? That is why your feet seem so glad and your anklets jingle so merrily as you walk.”"},{"id":"C","content":"“I’ll pay when I grow up—before I leave to look for work out on the other side of that stream there.”"},{"id":"D","content":"“Wish I could be out too. Then I would pick some flowers for you from the very topmost branches right out of sight.”"}]', explanation_html=NULL, stem_text='The Post Office is a 1912 play by Rabindranath Tagore. Amal imagines people passing his window are carefree even when working, as when he says to a flower seller''s daughter: ______ Which quotation from The Post Office most effectively illustrates the claim?' WHERE id='pt10_rw_m1_q12';
