ect x="224" y="176" width="32" height="64" fill="#777" stroke="#000"/><text x="223" y="256" font-size="11" text-anchor="middle">10</text><rect x="295" y="138" width="32" height="102" fill="#fff" stroke="#000"/><rect x="329" y="186" width="32" height="54" fill="#777" stroke="#000"/><text x="328" y="256" font-size="11" text-anchor="middle">20</text><rect x="400" y="154" width="32" height="86" fill="#fff" stroke="#000"/><rect x="434" y="194" width="32" height="46" fill="#777" stroke="#000"/><text x="433" y="256" font-size="11" text-anchor="middle">30</text><text x="275" y="274" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle">Day of experiment</text><text x="16" y="140" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" transform="rotate(-90 16 140)">Spider count</text><rect x="300" y="36" width="14" height="12" fill="#fff" stroke="#000"/><text x="320" y="46" font-size="11">no lizards</text><rect x="390" y="36" width="14" height="12" fill="#777" stroke="#000"/><text x="410" y="46" font-size="11">with lizards</text></svg></figure><p>To investigate the effect of lizard predation on spider populations, a student in a biology class placed spiders in two enclosures, one with lizards and one without, and tracked the number of spiders in the enclosures for 30 days. The student concluded that the reduction in the spider population count in the enclosure with lizards by day 30 was entirely attributable to the presence of the lizards.</p><p>Which choice best describes data from the graph that weaken the student&rsquo;s conclusion?</p>', choices_json='[{"id": "A", "content": "Spider count was the same in both enclosures on day 1."}, {"id": "B", "content": "Spider count also substantially declined by day 30 in the enclosure without lizards."}, {"id": "C", "content": "The largest decline in the lizard enclosure occurred from day 1 to day 10."}, {"id": "D", "content": "Spider count on day 30 was lower in the lizard enclosure than the no-lizard enclosure."}]', explanation_html=NULL, stem_text='Spider Population Count01020304050607080901102030Day of experimentSpider countno lizardswith lizardsTo investigate the effect of lizard predation on spider populations, a student in a biology class placed spiders in two enclosures, one with lizards and one without, and tracked the number of spiders in the enclosures for 30 days. The student concluded that the reduction in the spider population count in the enclosure with lizards by day 30 was entirely attributable to the presence of the lizards.
Which choice best describes data from the graph that weaken the student&rsquo;s conclusion?' WHERE id='pt10_rw_m1_q13';
