UPDATE questions SET stem_html='<p><em>Adapted from</em> Indian Boyhood, <em>a 1902 memoir by Ohiyesa (Charles A. Eastman), a Santee Dakota writer. Ohiyesa recalls how the women in his tribe harvested maple syrup.</em></p><p>Now the women began to test the trees&mdash;moving leisurely among them, axe in hand, and striking a single quick blow, to see if the sap would appear. <u>The trees, like people, have their individual characters; some were ready to yield up their life-blood, while others were more reluctant.</u> Now one of the birchen basins was set under each tree, and a hardwood chip driven deep into the cut which the axe had made. From the corners of this chip&mdash;at first drop by drop, then more freely&mdash;the sap trickled into the little dishes.</p><p><strong>Which choice best describes the function of the underlined sentence in the text as a whole?</strong></p>', choices_json='[{"id": "A", "content": "It portrays the range of personality traits displayed by the women as they work."}, {"id": "B", "content": "It foregrounds the beneficial relationship between humans and maple trees."}, {"id": "C", "content": "It demonstrates how human behavior can be influenced by the natural environment."}, {"id": "D", "content": "It elaborates on an aspect of the maple trees that the women evaluate."}]', explanation_html=NULL, stem_text='Adapted from Indian Boyhood, a 1902 memoir by Ohiyesa (Charles A. Eastman), a Santee Dakota writer. Ohiyesa recalls how the women in his tribe harvested maple syrup.
Now the women began to test the trees&mdash;moving leisurely among them, axe in hand, and striking a single quick blow, to see if the sap would appear. The trees, like people, have their individual characters; some were ready to yield up their life-blood, while others were more reluctant. Now one of the birchen basins was set under each tree, and a hardwood chip driven deep into the cut which the axe had made. From the corners of this chip&mdash;at first drop by drop, then more freely&mdash;the sap trickled into the little dishes.
Which choice best describes the function of the underlined sentence in the text as a whole?' WHERE id='pt4_rw_m2_q5';
UPDATE questions SET stem_html='<p>While attending school in New York City in the 1980s, Okwui Enwezor encountered few works by African artists in exhibitions, despite New York''s reputation as one of the best places to view contemporary art from around the world. According to an arts journalist, later in his career as a renowned curator and art historian, Enwezor sought to remedy this deficiency, <strong>not by focusing solely on modern African artists, but by showing how their work fits into the larger context of global modern art and art history</strong>.</p><p><strong>Which finding, if true, would most directly support the journalist''s claim?</strong></p>', choices_json='[{"id": "A", "content": "As curator of the Haus der Kunst in Munich, Enwezor organized a retrospective of Ghanaian sculptor El Anatsui''s work, one of the largest exhibitions devoted to a Black artist in Europe''s history."}, {"id": "B", "content": "In Postwar: Art Between the Pacific and the Atlantic, 1945-1965, Enwezor and cocurator Katy Siegel brought works by African artists such as Malangatana Ngwenya together with pieces by major figures from other countries, like US artist Andy Warhol and Mexico''s David Siqueiros."}, {"id": "C", "content": "Enwezor''s work as curator of The Short Century: Independence and Liberation Movements in Africa, 1945-1994 showed how African independence movements profoundly influenced work by African artists of the period, such as Kamala Ibrahim Ishaq and Thomas Mukarobgwa."}, {"id": "D", "content": "Enwezor organized In/sight: African Photographers, 1940 to the Present not to emphasize a particular aesthetic trend but to demonstrate the broad range of ways African artists have approached photography."}]', explanation_html=NULL, stem_text='While attending school in New York City in the 1980s, Okwui Enwezor encountered few works by African artists in exhibitions, despite New York''s reputation as one of the best places to view contemporary art from around the world. According to an arts journalist, later in his career as a renowned curator and art historian, Enwezor sought to remedy this deficiency, not by focusing solely on modern African artists, but by showing how their work fits into the larger context of global modern art and art history.
Which finding, if true, would most directly support the journalist''s claim?' WHERE id='pt4_rw_m2_q14';
UPDATE questions SET stem_html='<p>One challenge when researching whether holding elected office changes a person''s behavior is the problem of ensuring that the experiment has an appropriate control group. To reveal the effect of holding office, researchers must compare people who hold elected office with people who do not hold office but who are otherwise similar to the office-holders. Since researchers are unable to control which politicians win elections, they therefore ______</p><p><strong>Which choice most logically completes the text?</strong></p>', choices_json='[{"id": "A", "content": "struggle to find valid data about the behavior of politicians who do not currently hold office."}, {"id": "B", "content": "can only conduct valid studies with people who have previously held office rather than people who presently hold office."}, {"id": "C", "content": "should select a control group of people who differ from office-holders in several significant ways."}, {"id": "D", "content": "will find it difficult to identify a group of people who can function as an appropriate control group for their studies."}]', explanation_html=NULL, stem_text='One challenge when researching whether holding elected office changes a person''s behavior is the problem of ensuring that the experiment has an appropriate control group. To reveal the effect of holding office, researchers must compare people who hold elected office with people who do not hold office but who are otherwise similar to the office-holders. Since researchers are unable to control which politicians win elections, they therefore ______
Which choice most logically completes the text?' WHERE id='pt4_rw_m2_q15';
UPDATE questions SET stem_html='<p>Compiled in the late 1500s largely through the efforts of Indigenous scribes, Cantares Mexicanos is the most important collection of poetry in Classical Nahuatl, the principal language of the Aztec Empire. The poems portray Aztec society before the occupation of the empire by the army of Spain, and marginal notes in Cantares Mexicanos indicate that much of the collection''s content <strong>predates the initial invasion</strong>. <strong>Nonetheless</strong>, some of the poems contain <strong>inarguable</strong> references to beliefs and customs common in Spain during this era. Thus, some scholars have concluded that ______</p><p><strong>Which choice most logically completes the text?</strong></p>', choices_json='[{"id": "A", "content": "while its content largely predates the invasion, Cantares Mexicanos also contains additions made after the invasion."}, {"id": "B", "content": "although those who compiled Cantares Mexicanos were fluent in Nahuatl, they had limited knowledge of the Spanish language."}, {"id": "C", "content": "before the invasion by Spain, the poets of the Aztec Empire borrowed from the literary traditions of other societies."}, {"id": "D", "content": "the references to beliefs and customs in Spain should be attributed to a coincidental resemblance between the societies of Spain and the Aztec Empire."}]', explanation_html=NULL, stem_text='Compiled in the late 1500s largely through the efforts of Indigenous scribes, Cantares Mexicanos is the most important collection of poetry in Classical Nahuatl, the principal language of the Aztec Empire. The poems portray Aztec society before the occupation of the empire by the army of Spain, and marginal notes in Cantares Mexicanos indicate that much of the collection''s content predates the initial invasion. Nonetheless, some of the poems contain inarguable references to beliefs and customs common in Spain during this era. Thus, some scholars have concluded that ______
Which choice most logically completes the text?' WHERE id='pt4_rw_m2_q16';
